\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Opposite scalings in adjacent degrees}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [two first-order cochain operators](fdip-00SR)
connect degrees of opposite parity. In a bilinear term, a
factor #{u} at one end can cancel a factor #{u^{-1}} at the
other. The paired top word, however, uses every generator
once. How does this simultaneous scaling act on the
[ring paired coefficient](fdip-00TJ), especially when the
numbers of even and odd cells differ?}
